TITLE:: PnumSeq
SUMMARY:: A fixed registry of ten mathematical sequences
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events>Patterns>Patternarium
RELATED:: Classes/Pscan, Classes/ProtationWord, Classes/Pmorphism

DESCRIPTION::
Yields Integers, except calkinWilf yields fresh numerator/denominator Arrays and lookAndSay yields fresh decimal digit Arrays. Sequence state is newly allocated per stream. Names are Symbols and the registry cannot be changed. Unknown names and unsupported seeds/options throw descriptive Errors.

Recaman, vanEck, paperfolding, rudinShapiro, stern and norgard start at index zero. Golomb, Kolakoski and Calkin-Wilf use their standard first term; lookAndSay outputs its seed as the first term. All seeds are literal objects or Functions evaluated once with inval. No seed Pattern evaluation is advertised.

Unbounded streams can consume unbounded memory for history-dependent sequences. Look-and-say checks maxTermSize before extending a term. Kolakoski accepts two distinct positive Integer run symbols, each at most 1000000. Its canonical bootstrap is the first symbol repeated that many times; when the first symbol is 1, the second run is also bootstrapped. Default alphabet [1,2] gives the standard word. Seeds are deliberately restricted to the documented sequences.

Integer outputs that would exceed 2147483647 throw; output indices are also bounded to avoid signed Integer overflow. These are exact machine-integer streams, not arbitrary-precision arithmetic.

TABLE::
## Name ## First output / definition ## Seed / options ## Memory
## recaman ## 0; subtract index if nonnegative and unseen, else add ## nonnegative Integer seed, default 0 ## O(distinct visited values)
## vanEck ## 0; distance to the previous occurrence of the last value, else 0 ## nonempty nonnegative Integer seed collection, default [0]; seed items are output first ## O(distinct values)
## golomb ## 1,2,2; a(n) counts occurrences of n, indexed from 1 ## nil seed only ## O(outputs)
## kolakoski ## 1,2,2,1; the word describes its own run lengths ## nil seed; alphabet option defaults to [1,2] ## O(outputs plus bootstrap)
## paperfolding ## 1,1,0; odd part of n+1 is 1 mod 4 ## nil seed only ## O(1)
## rudinShapiro ## 1,1,1,-1; parity of overlapping 11 pairs in binary n ## nil seed; binary true maps +1 to 0 and -1 to 1 ## O(1)
## stern ## 0,1,1,2; s(2n)=s(n), s(2n+1)=s(n)+s(n+1) ## nil seed only ## O(1)
## calkinWilf ## [1,1], [1,2], [2,1]; breadth-first rational enumeration ## nil seed only ## O(1)
## lookAndSay ## [1], [1,1], [2,1]; decimal run-length description ## nonempty digit seed, default [1]; maxTermSize default 100000 ## O(maxTermSize)
## norgard ## 0,1,-1,2; a(2n)=-a(n), a(2n+1)=a(n)+1 ## nil seed only ## O(log(index)) transient digits
::


CLASSMETHODS::
METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: name
Supported Symbol, Function or Pattern sampled once at stream start. See names.
ARGUMENT:: seed
Nil by default; only recaman, vanEck and lookAndSay accept non-nil seeds. Evaluated once with value(inval); copied where mutable.
ARGUMENT:: length
Nonnegative Integer or inf, default inf; literal, Function or Pattern sampled once.
ARGUMENT:: options
Literal Dictionary or Event, default empty. Only per-sequence options shown above are accepted.

METHOD:: names
Returns a fresh Array of the ten supported Symbols. Changing it cannot change dispatch.

INSTANCEMETHODS::
METHOD:: storeArgs
Returns constructor arguments.
METHOD:: embedInStream
Yields values and returns the latest inval on termination.

EXAMPLES::
code::
PnumSeq(\recaman, length: 16).asStream.all;
::

Pitch follows the output; repeated phrases make the structure audible. Uses the instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments::.
code::
(
// Sound companion: PnumSeq / Value stream
var values = {
PnumSeq(\recaman, length: 16).asStream.all;
}.value;
values = if(values.isArray) { values } { [values] };
Pseq(values, 4).keep(64).collect { |x|
    (instrument: \fmPiano, degree: (x % 14)-3, dur: 0.18, amp: 0.08)
}.play;
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Musical mapping
Load the example instruments in link::Guides/Patternarium#Example instruments:: first.
code::
(
Pbind(\instrument, \mallet, \degree, PnumSeq(\norgard, length: 32).collect { |x| x.fold(-7, 7) }, \dur, 0.125).play;
)
::

